# Post-shipping workflow

After a project's deliverables ship, three prompts harvest what the project
produced: concepts/intuition → my knowledge repo, reusable code → my cookbook,
and systemic lessons → econ-templates itself. This rule wires the triggers.

## Precondition gate (check before running any of these)

Post-shipping runs only when the project is genuinely DONE:
- The planned outputs are in `outputs/figures/` and `outputs/processed/`.
- The `40-validate.mdc` gates pass.
- I've reviewed the figures and I'm happy.
- If this project distributes (email/commentary), the `60-post-analysis.mdc`
  send already happened — post-shipping is *after* the deliverable went out.

If any of these isn't true, STOP and tell me — don't harvest an unfinished
project.

## Triggers

| I type | You run |
|---|---|
| **"post-ship"** (or "wrap project") | all three prompts, in order, one at a time |
| **"distill"** (or "harvest concepts") | `@C:/Users/asingh/new_work/econ-templates/prompts/knowledge_distillation.md` only |
| **"capture patterns"** (or "harvest code") | `@C:/Users/asingh/new_work/econ-templates/prompts/code_patterns_capture.md` only |
| **"port lessons"** (or "harvest lessons") | `@C:/Users/asingh/new_work/econ-templates/prompts/lessons_to_templates.md` only |

## "post-ship" sequence

Run the three **one by one**, in this order, and do not start the next until
the current one is fully done (through all its own STOP gates and my approvals):

1. **knowledge_distillation.md** — concepts/intuition → `knowledge_repo`.
   Independent of the others; first because it's pure harvest.
2. **code_patterns_capture.md** — reusable code → `knowledge_repo/code-cookbook`.
   Must run before step 3: it produces the `template_worthy` hand-off list that
   step 3 consumes.
3. **lessons_to_templates.md** — systemic lessons → `econ-templates` files
   (with human-approval discipline; pre-commit review before any push).

Before each step, announce which prompt is starting and read its full text via
the `@`-path above. Honor every STOP gate inside each prompt — "post-ship" is a
convenience wrapper, not a license to skip approvals. If I only want one part,
I'll use the single-prompt trigger instead.

## What this rule does NOT do

- It doesn't override any STOP gate or approval inside the three prompts.
- It doesn't auto-push: `knowledge_repo` commits and any `econ-templates` edits
  are staged and surfaced for my review first.
- It doesn't run on an unfinished project — see the precondition gate.
